@node LibreClaw Overview
@section Overview

LibreClaw is a GObject-native AI agent gateway, written in C with
GLib/GObject, that routes messages between AI sessions and messaging
channels.  It talks Matrix via libsoup3, accepts stdin/stdout for
local CLI, speaks IMAP/SMTP through libetpan for email, hosts HTTP
webhook receivers, and dispatches to Claude or OpenAI via ai-glib.

@subsection Why embed it in cmacs

@enumerate
@item
Native GObject — fits cmacs's GLib-based architecture cleanly.
@item
Shared main loop — libreclaw 0.18.0 added embed mode
(@code{lc_app_new_embedded}) that attaches sources to any
GMainContext without owning a GMainLoop, so Emacs's pselect-based
loop drives everything.
@item
Shared podomation — 0.18.0 added @code{lc_podomation_new_with_engine}
so libreclaw reuses cmacs's PodEngine instead of running a second
one.  DSL rules defined in either place see each other.
@item
Org-mode buffers — treating each room as an org document means users
get multi-line editing, source blocks, tables, links, and attachments
for free.
@end enumerate

@subsection Lifecycle

@enumerate
@item
User sets @code{cmacs-libreclaw-config-file} to a YAML path.
@item
User runs @kbd{M-x cmacs-libreclaw-start}.
@item
@file{cmacs-libreclaw.el} ensures @code{cmacs-podomation} is running,
then calls the C DEFUN @code{cmacs-libreclaw--start-internal}.
@item
The C layer registers the @code{pod-cmacs-libreclaw-module} on the
shared engine, calls @code{lc_app_new_embedded} with the config path
and shared engine, calls @code{lc_app_start_embedded} to bring up
components, and wires @file{cmacs-libreclaw-room.c} signal handlers
into @code{LcChannelManager::message-received} and related events.
@item
Incoming messages fire C callbacks, which format a Lisp expression
and hand it to @code{cmacs_dispatch_eval} — the same mechanism
@file{pod-cmacs-module.c} uses to stay safe across the
@code{waiting_for_input} invariant.
@item
Elisp inserts the message into the appropriate room buffer as a new
level-2 org heading above the @samp{* Compose} sentinel.
@item
User types a response below @samp{* Compose} and presses @kbd{C-c C-c}.
@code{cmacs-libreclaw-send-compose} grabs the region and calls
@code{cmacs-libreclaw-send-message}, which async-queues the send.
@end enumerate
